{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.BondFactorClassicalFloor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.BondFactorClassicalFloor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UrsellPartitionFunctionB3","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.b3_bondModel_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.b3_bondModel_classical","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L94-L99","doc":"Assembled: the classical three-body cumulant of the bond model, with every\nbond factor evaluated at the classical point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.phi3_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.phi3_classical","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L90-L92","doc":"The same statement through the Ursell function: `φᵀ₃(−1/2, −1/2, −1/2) = 5/8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.b3corpus_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.b3corpus_classical","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L83-L88","doc":"**The connected three-body cumulant does not vanish at `q = 1`:** `b₃ = −5/8`.\nHence its `ε`-valuation is `0`, and the body-number expansion carries no power\ncounting in `ε`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:body-number-expansion-classical-floor","label":"rem:body-number-expansion-classical-floor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/body-number-expansion-classical-floor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.mayer_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.mayer_classical","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L79-L81","doc":"The Mayer variable of a classical bond is `−1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondFactor_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondFactor_classical","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L75-L77","doc":"**Every bond factor is `1/2` at the classical point**, whatever its kind. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.bondFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.bondFactor","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L72-L73","doc":"The bond factor `z_D(1 + ε) + d_kind(ε)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.dKind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.dKind","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L65-L70","doc":"The kind-dependent correction `d_kind(ε)`, the probe's measured series truncated\nat second order: `0`, `−ε + ε²/2`, `−2ε + ε²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind.nn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind.nn","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind.pn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind.pn","kind":"ctor","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind.pp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind.pp","kind":"ctor","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.InterfaceKind","kind":"inductive","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L59-L63","doc":"The three interface kinds of the canonical atom word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.zD_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.zD_one","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L55-L57","doc":"**At the classical point the Markov parameter is `1/2`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.zD","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/BondFactorClassicalFloor.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q² + 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}